    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Bryce Harper** (75.45) anchors our lineup as the premier play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Phillips and a high-leverage #3 spot in the order. His elite xwOBA metrics remain the engine of our scoring. **Dylan Beavers** (69.51) and **Luis Arraez** (66.61) follow closely behind; both are massive beneficiaries of the favorable wind conditions and optimal leadoff positioning against their respective starters. **Geraldo Perdomo** (64.76) also projects as an excellent start despite a standard matchup, as his jump to the #2 spot significantly boosts his scoring potential, providing a necessary bridge for our power-heavy middle order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Ryan Waldschmidt** (49.67). While he offers decent utility, the move to the #9 hole against Keller pushed his efficiency score below the threshold required to displace our current starters. We are prioritizing the higher ceiling offered by **Jeremiah Jackson** (58.22) and **Taylor Ward** (58.74) due to the wind-out conditions at their park, which mathematically outweighs the raw base projections of our bench assets. \n\nWe are monitoring the status of **Yainer Diaz**, as his score of 60.95 is predicated on an assumed #6 spot in the lineup. Should his actual placement drift lower, his utility will drop accordingly. Additionally, while we like the platoon edge for **Daulton Varsho** (57.71), we are proceeding with caution as his production against Yean remains our most volatile variable. We have opted to bench **Lawrence Butler** (44.29) and **Braden Montgomery** (43.76) as both face sub-4.00 xERA pitchers, confirming that today\u2019s roster construction is prioritized strictly on efficiency and hitting environment.",
